# Phaser Audio Performance Optimization

## Context
- When implementing high-action gameplay with many sound effects
- When optimizing for mobile devices with limited audio capabilities
- When experiencing audio-related performance issues
- When implementing sound-heavy games

## Requirements
- Use Phaser's built-in audio pooling for frequently played sounds
- Implement audio sprites for short, frequent sound effects
- Apply sound rate limiting for repetitive effects
- Use priority-based sound playing for high-action sequences
- Implement distance-based audio culling for spatial sounds

## Examples

```typescript
// Audio manager with performance optimizations
export class OptimizedAudioManager {
  private scene: Phaser.Scene;
  private soundPools: Map<string, Phaser.Sound.BaseSound[]> = new Map();
  private audioSprites: Map<string, Phaser.Sound.BaseSound> = new Map();
  
  // Sound rate limiting to prevent audio clutter
  private soundTimestamps: Map<string, number> = new Map();
  private soundCooldowns: Map<string, number> = new Map();
  
  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {
    this.scene = scene;
    
    // Set up sound cooldowns for rate limiting
    this.soundCooldowns.set('shoot', 50);  // 50ms between shots
    this.soundCooldowns.set('footstep', 200); // 200ms between steps
    
    // Create pools for frequently used sounds
    this.createSoundPool('shoot', 5);
    this.createSoundPool('explosion', 3);
    
    // Create audio sprite
    this.createAudioSprite('sfxSprite');
  }
  
  /**
   * Create a pool of sound instances for frequent sounds
   */
  private createSoundPool(key: string, size: number): void {
    const pool: Phaser.Sound.BaseSound[] = [];
    
    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) {
      const sound = this.scene.sound.add(key, { loop: false });
      pool.push(sound);
    }
    
    this.soundPools.set(key, pool);
  }
  
  /**
   * Create and configure an audio sprite
   */
  private createAudioSprite(key: string): void {
    const sprite = this.scene.sound.addAudioSprite(key);
    if (sprite) {
      this.audioSprites.set(key, sprite);
    }
  }
  
  /**
   * Play a sound from a pool with rate limiting
   */
  playSoundFromPool(key: string): void {
    // Skip if on cooldown
    const now = this.scene.time.now;
    const lastPlayed = this.soundTimestamps.get(key) || 0;
    const cooldown = this.soundCooldowns.get(key) || 0;
    
    if (now - lastPlayed < cooldown) {
      return; // Still on cooldown
    }
    
    // Get sound pool
    const pool = this.soundPools.get(key);
    if (!pool || pool.length === 0) return;
    
    // Find available sound in pool
    let sound = pool.find(s => !s.isPlaying);
    
    // If all sounds are playing, pick the oldest one
    if (!sound) {
      let oldestTime = Infinity;
      let oldestSound = null;
      
      pool.forEach(s => {
        if (s.isPlaying) {
          const startTime = s.data?.get('startTime') || 0;
          if (startTime < oldestTime) {
            oldestTime = startTime;
            oldestSound = s;
          }
        }
      });
      
      sound = oldestSound;
      if (sound) sound.stop();
    }
    
    // Play the sound and track timestamp
    if (sound) {
      sound.play();
      sound.data = sound.data || new Phaser.Data.DataManager({});
      sound.data.set('startTime', now);
      this.soundTimestamps.set(key, now);
    }
  }
  
  /**
   * Play a sound from an audio sprite
   */
  playSpriteSound(spriteKey: string, soundKey: string): void {
    const sprite = this.audioSprites.get(spriteKey);
    if (sprite) {
      (sprite as Phaser.Sound.WebAudioSound).play(soundKey);
    }
  }
  
  /**
   * Play sound with distance-based volume for spatial audio
   */
  playSpatialSound(key: string, x: number, y: number, maxDistance: number = 300): void {
    // Get player position (assuming it's stored in a game object)
    const player = this.scene.player;
    if (!player) return;
    
    // Calculate distance to sound source
    const dx = player.x - x;
    const dy = player.y - y;
    const distance = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
    
    // Skip if too far
    if (distance > maxDistance) return;
    
    // Calculate volume based on distance (inverse linear falloff)
    const volume = 1 - (distance / maxDistance);
    
    // Play with calculated volume
    this.scene.sound.play(key, { volume });
  }
}
```

## Audio Pooling
- Create pools for frequently played sounds
- Reuse sound instances instead of creating new ones
- Track which sounds in the pool are currently playing
- Select the oldest playing sound when all are in use

## Audio Sprites
- Combine small sound effects into a single audio file
- Reduce the number of audio file loads
- Use spritemap JSON to define sound markers
- Play individual sounds from the sprite using markers

## Rate Limiting
- Set cooldown periods for frequently triggered sounds
- Skip sound playback when still on cooldown
- Vary cooldown time based on sound importance
- Maintain separate cooldowns for different sound categories

